{
  "name": "Unknown Write · 2 Check",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Unknown Write · Check\nRuns every minute and works through the rows that are still open. All state is in the data table, so nothing is lost when n8n restarts, and no execution sits in a Wait node.\n\nFor each open job that is due:\n1. **Look it up** by the reference. Exactly one record with an id: `done`. Anything else (404, an empty or odd 200, an error) is **no evidence** and changes nothing.\n2. No evidence, job not yet with a person: **ask for a receipt**. Only a receipt that names this reference and this attempt, is terminal and says `not_applied` allows one more write. The resend is claimed in the row first.\n3. Otherwise count the check. After the last entry of `RECHECK_AFTER_SECONDS` the job goes to `review` and an alert is sent.\n4. Jobs in `review` are still looked up, every `REVIEW_RECHECK_SECONDS`. If the record shows up late, the job is closed and a second alert says so. A job in `review` is never written again by this workflow.\n\nSettings are at the top of **Settings**. Replace **Look it up** and **Ask for a receipt** with your own requests and adapt the two **Judge** nodes to what your API returns. No receipt endpoint: set `USE_RECEIPT` to false and nothing is ever sent twice.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 500,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "63f0ce79-4266-4329-8de0-0d9143d83cf1",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -680
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 1
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "2fefa131-9a84-47cd-8b96-52854115ca51",
      "name": "Every minute",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        0,
        -80
      ]
    },
